Package: inari
Architecture: amd64 arm64
# The binary is statically linked, so it needs nothing at run time. systemd is
# a Recommends rather than a Depends on purpose: the unit is the supported way
# to run this, but the binary is perfectly usable without it, and a hard
# dependency would make the package refuse to configure anywhere systemd is
# absent -- including a container, where that failure also skips the postinst
# that generates the session secret.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: systemd
Description: Manage S3-compatible object storage
 Inari is a web service for browsing and managing S3-compatible object
 storage. Every storage operation runs server-side; credentials are supplied
 by the user at connect time and sealed in an encrypted, http-only cookie that
 only the server can decrypt.
 .
 The package installs a single static binary with the web interface compiled
 in, so it has no runtime dependencies. The service is left stopped after
 installation because it needs an endpoint configured first; see
 /usr/share/doc/inari/README.Debian.
